course: dictionary
lesson: 4713
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Hook is one of them. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. «Hang your coat on the hook by the door» tells you a hook is something you hang things on.
explain: Other sentences show other meanings. «A fish hook stuck in a finger is not pulled out» is about a fishing hook, a small sharp curved piece of metal that catches fish. «Eagles are big birds of prey with hooked beaks» means their beaks are curved like a hook.
explain: Writers use hook in a special way too. In a story, the hook is the opening sentence that grabs your interest and makes you want to read on. Ask yourself: which meaning fits here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A hook is a curved or bent piece of metal or plastic.
fact: Hook can be a noun (a hook) or a verb (to hook something, to catch or fasten it).
fact: A fishing hook is sharp and has a barb, a little backward hook that makes it hard to pull out of skin. An adult should help remove it.
fact: In a story, the hook is the opening that grabs the reader.
fact: «Off the hook» means free from trouble. «Hooked on» means you love something so much you cannot stop.
exercise: «Hang your coat on the hook by the door.» What is a hook in this sentence? | A loud noise | *A bent piece of metal or plastic for hanging things on | A short story | A fish that lives in the sea
exercise: «The first sentence is the hook, and it grabs the reader.» What does hook mean here? | A kind of bird | A tool for digging | *The part that catches your interest | A slow walk
exercise: «Eagles are big birds of prey with hooked beaks.» What does hooked mean? | Sweet smelling | Lost and empty | Very loud | *Curved like a hook
test: «A fish hook stuck in a finger is not pulled out by you; an adult or doctor removes it.» Why should an adult help? | Because it is a game | Because the hook is too big to see | Because fish hooks are soft | *Because the barb tears skin
test: «An anchor is a heavy shaped hook that digs into the seabed.» What is an anchor? | A light sail for a boat | A kind of fish | *A heavy hook that digs into the seabed | A rope knot used for tying shoes
exam: Which phrase means free from trouble? | By hook or by crook | On the hook | Hook up | *Off the hook
